{"schema_version":1,"source_commit":"100560de6c9f68c2875097d40a2012a84c784179","scope":"Śrīmad-Bhāgavatam Canto 2, Chapter 1 — Śrīdhara Svāmī word-for-word gloss","source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/01_dhyAnavidhiH.md","source_blob_sha":"14edc4de01f9e540a6c72dbdd4e4cfa009224c3c","entries":[{"canto":2,"chapter":1,"start":1,"end":1,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/01_dhyAnavidhiH.md","source_blob_sha":"14edc4de01f9e540a6c72dbdd4e4cfa009224c3c","pairs":[["श्री-गणेशाय नमः","obeisance to Śrī Gaṇeśa"],["द्वितीये तु","in the second [canto]"],["दशाध्यायैः","in ten chapters"],["श्री-भागवतम्","the Śrī-Bhāgavata"],["आदितः","from its beginning"],["उद्देश-लक्षणोक्तिभ्याम्","through statements of enumeration and defining characteristics"],["सङ्क्षेपेण","in brief"],["उपवर्ण्यते","is described"],["तत्र तु प्रथमेऽध्याये","there, in the first chapter"],["कीर्तन-श्रवणादिभिः","by praise, hearing and related practices"],["स्थविष्ठे भगवद्-रूपे","upon the Lord's vast or gross form"],["मनसो धारणोच्यते","fixing of the mind"],["यन्-नाम-कीर्तनं","the recitation of whose name"],["दान-तपो-योगादि सत्-फलम्","is the good fruit of giving, austerity, yoga and the like"],["तं","him"],["नित्यं","eternal"],["परमानन्दं","supreme bliss"],["हरिं","Hari"],["नर","O man"],["नम","bow to"],["स्मर","remember"],["अथ","now"],["द्वितीय-स्कन्ध-व्याख्या","the commentary on the second canto"],["उक्तः पूर्वम्","previously described"],["उपोद्घातः","the introduction"],["सप्रसङ्गः","with its accompanying context"],["शुकागमः","the arrival of Śuka"],["राज्ञा पृष्टं","asked by the king"],["नॄणां कृत्यम्","what human beings should do"],["अथाह","now he states"],["शुक-सन्-मुनिः","Śuka, the noble sage"],["राज्ञः प्रश्नम्","the king's question"],["अभिनन्दति","he commends"],["वरीयान् इति","with the verse beginning ‘more excellent’"],["ते","by you"],["त्वया","by you"],["पुंसां श्रोतव्यादिषु मध्ये","among things that people should hear and the rest"],["यः परः","that which is highest"],["श्रेष्ठ-गोचरः","having the supreme as its subject"],["प्रश्नः कृतः","the question that has been asked"],["एष वरीयान्","this is especially excellent"],["यतः","because"],["लोक-हितम् एतत्","it benefits the world"],["मोक्ष-हेतुत्वात्","because it brings about liberation"],["आत्म-विदां","of those who know the self"],["मुक्तानां च","and of the liberated"],["संमतो","approved or esteemed"],["यतः","because"]],"note":"Opening Śrīdhara invocation and commentary on 2.1.1; source phrases were checked against the pinned chapter file."},{"canto":2,"chapter":1,"start":2,"end":2,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/01_dhyAnavidhiH.md","source_blob_sha":"14edc4de01f9e540a6c72dbdd4e4cfa009224c3c","pairs":[["तत्र तावत्","There, first"],["स्वाभाविक-क्रियाणाम्","of habitual activities"],["अनर्थ-हेतुत्वं वदन्","while describing their being causes of misfortune"],["ब्रूहि यद् वा विपर्ययं इत्य् अस्योत्तरम् आह","he answers the earlier request beginning ‘Tell [me] what, instead, is the opposite’"],["श्रोतव्यादीनीति त्रिभिः","with three verses beginning ‘Things to be heard,’ and so on"],["गृहेषु सक्तानाम्","of those attached to their homes"],["अत एव","and for that very reason"],["गृह-मेधिनाम्","of those engaged in household life, glossed through the root medh"],["तद्-गत-पञ्च-सूना-पराणाम्","of those involved in its five household sources of injury"],["मेधतिर् हिंसार्थः","the verb medh has the meaning ‘to injure’"]],"note":"Existing reviewed wording retained after comparison with the pinned Śrīdhara block at 2.1.2."},{"canto":2,"chapter":1,"start":3,"end":3,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/01_dhyAnavidhiH.md","source_blob_sha":"14edc4de01f9e540a6c72dbdd4e4cfa009224c3c","pairs":[["तैश् च श्रोतव्य-जाप्यादिभिः","and by hearing, recitation, and related practices"],["वृथैवायुर् व्ययो भवति","life is wasted in vain"],["नक्तं रात्रौ","at night"],["यद् वय आयुस्","whatever portion of life"],["तन् निद्रया व्यवायेन रत्या वा ह्रियते","is taken away by sleep, sex, or sensual pleasure"],["दिवा अह्नि","during the day"],["अर्थार्थम् उद्यमेन","by laboring for wealth"],["सिद्धेऽर्थे कुटुम्ब-पोषणेन वेति","or, once wealth is acquired, by maintaining the family"],["च-कारौ","the two particles ca"],["अनुक्त-समुच्चयार्थौ","express an addition of what has not been stated"]],"note":"Glosses Śrīdhara’s explanation of how life is spent at night and during the day; footnote 8 identifies the practices in ‘and by these.’"},{"canto":2,"chapter":1,"start":4,"end":4,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/01_dhyAnavidhiH.md","source_blob_sha":"14edc4de01f9e540a6c72dbdd4e4cfa009224c3c","pairs":[["नश्वर-कुटुम्बाद्य्-अर्थं","for the sake of perishable family and the like"],["कथम् आयुर्-व्ययं कुर्यात्","how should one spend one’s life in this way?"],["देहादिषु","in the body and the rest"],["आत्मनः सैन्येषु परिकरेष्व्","as one’s troops and attendants"],["असत्सु मिथ्या-भूतेष्व् अपि","although unreal and temporary"],["प्रमत्तः प्रसक्तः","heedless, attached"],["पित्रादि-दृष्टान्तेन","by examples such as one’s father"],["नाशं पश्यन्न् अपि","even while seeing their destruction"],["नानुसन्धत्ते","he does not reflect on it"]],"note":""},{"canto":2,"chapter":1,"start":5,"end":5,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/01_dhyAnavidhiH.md","source_blob_sha":"14edc4de01f9e540a6c72dbdd4e4cfa009224c3c","pairs":[["तस्मात्","therefore"],["हे भारत","O descendant of Bharata"],["सर्वात्मा","the Self of all"],["प्रेष्ठत्वम्","the quality of being most beloved"],["भगवान्","the beautiful Lord"],["ईश्वर","the indispensable Lord"],["हरिः","the remover of bondage"],["अभयं मोक्षम् इच्छता","by one desiring fearlessness, liberation"],["बन्ध-हारित्वम्","the state of removing bondage"]],"note":""},{"canto":2,"chapter":1,"start":6,"end":6,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/01_dhyAnavidhiH.md","source_blob_sha":"14edc4de01f9e540a6c72dbdd4e4cfa009224c3c","pairs":[["एतावान् एव जन्मनो लाभः","this alone is the gain of birth"],["नारायण-स्मृतिः","remembrance of Nārāyaṇa"],["साङ्ख्यादिभिः साध्यः","attainable through Sāṅkhya and the like"],["तेषां स्वातन्त्र्येण लाभत्वं वारयति","he rejects their being the independent goal"],["साङ्ख्यम् आत्मानात्म-विवेकः","Sāṅkhya is discrimination between self and non-self"],["योगोऽष्टाङ्गः","yoga is eight-limbed"],["अन्ते तु स्मृतिः परो लाभः","but remembrance at the end is the supreme gain"],["न तन्-महिमा वक्तुं शक्य","its greatness cannot be expressed"]],"note":""},{"canto":2,"chapter":1,"start":7,"end":7,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/01_dhyAnavidhiH.md","source_blob_sha":"14edc4de01f9e540a6c72dbdd4e4cfa009224c3c","pairs":[["सद्-आचारं प्रमाणयति","he establishes the authority of good conduct"],["विधि-षेधतो","through injunction and prohibition"],["विधि-निषेधाभ्यां निवृत्ताः","those withdrawn from prescribed and forbidden acts"],["नैर्गुण्ये ब्रह्मणि स्थिताः अपि","even those established in qualityless Brahman"],["स्म प्रसिद्धम्","this is well known"]],"note":""},{"canto":2,"chapter":1,"start":8,"end":8,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/01_dhyAnavidhiH.md","source_blob_sha":"14edc4de01f9e540a6c72dbdd4e4cfa009224c3c","pairs":[["इदम् अपूर्वम्","this is unprecedented"],["भगवत्-प्रोक्तम्","spoken by Bhagavān"],["तन्-नामैक-प्रधानं","having His name as its chief subject"],["पुराणम्","the Purāṇa"],["ब्रह्म-संमितं","equal in authority to the Vedas"],["ब्रह्म सम्यक् मितं येन","or, that by which Brahman is fully measured or known"],["अधीतवान् इति","‘he studied it’"],["द्वैपायनात् पितुः","from his father Dvaipāyana"],["द्वापरादौ","at the beginning of Dvāpara"],["द्वापरान्ते","at the end of Dvāpara"],["शन्तनु-सम-काले","at the time corresponding to Śantanu"],["व्यासावतार-प्रसिद्धेः","because Vyāsa’s incarnation is well known"]],"note":""},{"canto":2,"chapter":1,"start":9,"end":10,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/01_dhyAnavidhiH.md","source_blob_sha":"14edc4de01f9e540a6c72dbdd4e4cfa009224c3c","pairs":[["सिद्धस्य तव","of you, already perfected"],["कुतोऽध्ययने प्रवृत्तिः","why the engagement in study?"],["परिणिष्ठितोऽपि","although fully perfected"],["गृहीत-चेताः","with the mind captured"],["आकृष्ट-चित्तः","whose attention has been drawn"]],"note":"The pinned Śrīdhara source groups verses 2.1.9–10 in one commentary block; the WFW range preserves that grouping."},{"canto":2,"chapter":1,"start":11,"end":11,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/01_dhyAnavidhiH.md","source_blob_sha":"14edc4de01f9e540a6c72dbdd4e4cfa009224c3c","pairs":[["साधकानां सिद्धानां च","of seekers and of perfected beings"],["नातः परम् अन्यच्-छ्रेयः अस्ति","there is no higher good beyond this"],["इच्छतां कामिनाम्","for those who desire results"],["तत्-तत्-फल-साधनम्","a means of attaining each desired result"],["निर्विद्यमानानां मुमुक्षूणाम्","for those who are detached and seek liberation"],["मोक्ष-साधनम्","a means to liberation"],["योगिनां ज्ञानिनां फलं चैतद् एव","the result for yogīs and knowers"],["निर्णीतम्","is determined"],["नात्र प्रमाणं वक्तव्यम्","no proof need be stated here"]],"note":""},{"canto":2,"chapter":1,"start":12,"end":12,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/01_dhyAnavidhiH.md","source_blob_sha":"14edc4de01f9e540a6c72dbdd4e4cfa009224c3c","pairs":[["अल्पम् एव आयुर् अवशिष्टम्","only a little life remains"],["किमहं साधयेयम्","what can I accomplish?"],["मा शुचः","do not grieve"],["परोक्षैर् अलक्षितैर् हायनैर्","by years passing unnoticed"],["विदितम्","it is understood"],["वृथा याति","it passes in vain"],["यतो येन ज्ञानेन","by that knowledge"],["घटेत यत्नं कुर्यात्","one should make an effort"]],"note":""},{"canto":2,"chapter":1,"start":13,"end":13,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/01_dhyAnavidhiH.md","source_blob_sha":"14edc4de01f9e540a6c72dbdd4e4cfa009224c3c","pairs":[["खट्वाङ्गः","King Khaṭvāṅga"],["देव-पक्षे स्थित्वा","having taken the side of the gods"],["दैत्यान् अजयत्","he conquered the demons"],["वरं वृणीष्व","‘choose a boon’"],["प्रथमं तावन् ममायुः कथ्यताम्","‘first, tell me how long I shall live’"],["मुहूर्त-मात्रम् अस्ति","only a moment remains"],["अतिशीघ्रं विमानेन भुवम् आगत्य","having quickly reached earth in an airplane"],["हरिं शरणं गतः","he took refuge in Hari"]],"note":"The pinned source ends with visibly damaged readings “स्वर्ग-भुमी” and “कर्म-भूमिः प्र्थ्वी”. Those words are omitted here rather than silently reconstructed; the preceding Śrīdhara gloss is retained."},{"canto":2,"chapter":1,"start":14,"end":14,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/01_dhyAnavidhiH.md","source_blob_sha":"14edc4de01f9e540a6c72dbdd4e4cfa009224c3c","pairs":[["तव तु एतर्ह्य् अपीदानीम् अपि","but for you, even now"],["तावता कालेन","in that much time"],["साम्परायिकम्","pertaining to the next world"],["पारलौकिकं साधनम्","a means for the hereafter"],["सम्पादय","accomplish; prepare"]],"note":""},{"canto":2,"chapter":1,"start":15,"end":15,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/01_dhyAnavidhiH.md","source_blob_sha":"14edc4de01f9e540a6c72dbdd4e4cfa009224c3c","pairs":[["अन्त-काल इति","with the words ‘at the end of life’"],["गत-साध्वसः","free from fear of death"],["असङ्गो","nonattachment"],["अनासक्तिः","nonattachment"],["तेन शस्त्रेण","with that weapon"],["स्पृहां सुखेच्छां","desire for pleasure"],["तं देहम् अनु ये पुत्र-कलत्रादयस् तेष्व् अपि","those who follow the body, such as children and wife"],["तेष्व् अपि स्पृहाम्","desire for them as well"],["छिन्द्यात्","one should cut off"]],"note":""},{"canto":2,"chapter":1,"start":16,"end":17,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/01_dhyAnavidhiH.md","source_blob_sha":"14edc4de01f9e540a6c72dbdd4e4cfa009224c3c","pairs":[["गृहात् प्रव्रजितो निर्गतः","having gone forth from the home"],["गृहे स्थितस्य","for one remaining at home"],["आसक्ति-सम्भवात्","because attachment may arise"],["अष्टाङ्ग-योगम्","the eight-limbed yoga"],["धीरः","self-controlled"],["ब्रह्मचर्यादि-यम","the restraints beginning with celibacy"],["पुण्य-तीर्थ","holy places, indicating the observances"],["आसनम्","posture"],["शुचौ","in a clean place"],["विविक्ते एकान्ते","in a secluded, solitary place"],["विधिवत् कुशाजिन-चैलैः","properly arranged with kuśa grass, antelope skin, and cloth"],["जप-गर्भं प्राणायामं","breath control joined with mantra recitation"],["त्रिवृद्-ब्रह्माक्षरं","the threefold sacred syllable, Oṃ"],["अकारादिभिः","with the sounds beginning with a"],["मनसाऽभ्यसेद्","one should repeat mentally"],["मनो यच्छेत्","one should restrain the mind"],["ब्रह्म-बीजं प्रणवम्","Oṃ, the seed of Brahman"],["अविस्मरन्न् एव","without forgetting"],["जित-श्वासः सन्","while having controlled the breath"]],"note":"The pinned Śrīdhara source combines the commentary on 2.1.16–17; this WFW entry preserves the source range."},{"canto":2,"chapter":1,"start":18,"end":18,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/01_dhyAnavidhiH.md","source_blob_sha":"14edc4de01f9e540a6c72dbdd4e4cfa009224c3c","pairs":[["प्रत्याहारम्","withdrawal of the senses"],["नियच्छेत् निगृह्णीयात्","one should restrain"],["अक्षान् इन्द्रियाणि","the senses"],["निश्चयात्मिका बुद्धिः सारथिर् यस्य","whose charioteer is decisive intelligence"],["धारणाम्","concentration"],["कर्मभिः तद्-वासनाभिः","by actions and their latent impressions"],["आक्षिप्तम् आकृष्टम्","pulled and drawn"],["शुभार्थे भगवद्-रूपे","upon the auspicious form of Bhagavān"]],"note":""},{"canto":2,"chapter":1,"start":19,"end":19,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/01_dhyAnavidhiH.md","source_blob_sha":"14edc4de01f9e540a6c72dbdd4e4cfa009224c3c","pairs":[["ध्यानम्","meditation"],["तत्र","there; upon that"],["एकम् एकं-पादाद्य्-अवयवम्","one limb at a time, beginning with the feet"],["अव्युच्छिन्नेन","without interruption"],["समग्र-रूपाद् अवियुक्तेन","without separation from the complete form"],["चित्त-स्थिरीकरणम्","steadiness of mind"],["अवयव-विभावनया","by contemplation of the limbs"],["तद्-दार्ढ्यं ध्यानम्","its firmness is meditation"],["निर्विषयं मनो युंक्त्वा समाधाय","focusing and settling the mind free of objects"],["स्थिरीभूते मनसि","when the mind has become steady"],["स्फुरत्-परमानन्द-मात्राकारम्","having the form of manifest, pure supreme bliss"],["प्रसीदति उपशाम्यति","it becomes tranquil"]],"note":""},{"canto":2,"chapter":1,"start":20,"end":20,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/01_dhyAnavidhiH.md","source_blob_sha":"14edc4de01f9e540a6c72dbdd4e4cfa009224c3c","pairs":[["गुण-वशात्","under the influence of the qualities"],["क्षोभे सति","when agitation arises"],["धारणाम् एव स्थिरीकुर्यात्","one should steady concentration itself"],["रजसा आक्षिप्तम्","disturbed by passion"],["तमसा विमूढम्","bewildered by ignorance"],["स्वीयं मनो निरुन्ध्यात्","one should restrain one’s own mind"],["तत्-कृतम्","caused by that"],["रजस्-तमोभ्यां कृतम्","produced by passion and ignorance"]],"note":""},{"canto":2,"chapter":1,"start":21,"end":21,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/01_dhyAnavidhiH.md","source_blob_sha":"14edc4de01f9e540a6c72dbdd4e4cfa009224c3c","pairs":[["यतो यस्यां क्रियमाणायाम्","by which, while it is being practiced"],["भद्रं सुखात्मकम्","auspicious and of the nature of happiness"],["आश्रयं विषयम्","the supporting object"],["पश्यतः","for one who sees"],["तत्रैव प्रीतिर् भवति","affection arises right there"]],"note":""},{"canto":2,"chapter":1,"start":22,"end":22,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/01_dhyAnavidhiH.md","source_blob_sha":"14edc4de01f9e540a6c72dbdd4e4cfa009224c3c","pairs":[["यथा","how"],["यत्र यादृशी","where, and of what kind"],["चेतिकर्तव्यता-विषय","concerning the specifics of what is to be done"],["तत्-तद्-विशेषाणाम्","of those particular details"],["प्रश्नाः","questions"]],"note":""},{"canto":2,"chapter":1,"start":23,"end":23,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/01_dhyAnavidhiH.md","source_blob_sha":"14edc4de01f9e540a6c72dbdd4e4cfa009224c3c","pairs":[["यथेत्य् अस्योत्तरम्","the answer to ‘how’"],["जितासन इति","with the phrase ‘having mastered the posture’"],["विषयम् आह","he explains the object"],["स्थूल इति","with the word ‘gross’"],["स्थूले स्थविष्ठे विराड्-देहे","in the gross, most massive cosmic body"]],"note":""},{"canto":2,"chapter":1,"start":24,"end":24,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/01_dhyAnavidhiH.md","source_blob_sha":"14edc4de01f9e540a6c72dbdd4e4cfa009224c3c","pairs":[["विशेषो विराड्-देहः","the particular form is the cosmic body"],["अति-स्थूलानाम् अपि स्थूलतरः","more massive than even the very massive"],["सत् कार्य-मात्रम्","the entire effect, what exists"]],"note":""},{"canto":2,"chapter":1,"start":25,"end":25,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/01_dhyAnavidhiH.md","source_blob_sha":"14edc4de01f9e540a6c72dbdd4e4cfa009224c3c","pairs":[["अस्य उपलक्षणत्वेन विषयत्वम्","this is the object by way of an indicative representation"],["वस्तुतस् तु","but in reality"],["विराड्-जीव-नियन्ता भगवान् एव विषयः","the Lord, controller of the cosmic living being, is the true object"],["अण्ड-कोशान्तर्-वर्तिनि कटाहे","within the shell of the universe"],["पृथिव्य्-आवरणम्","the covering of the earth"],["अप्-तेजो-वाय्व्-आकाश-अहंकार-महत्-तत्त्वानि","water, fire, air, ether, ego, and the great principle"],["सप्त","seven"]],"note":""},{"canto":2,"chapter":1,"start":26,"end":26,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/01_dhyAnavidhiH.md","source_blob_sha":"14edc4de01f9e540a6c72dbdd4e4cfa009224c3c","pairs":[["विराड्-देह-तज्-जीव-तद्-अन्तर्यामिणाम्","of the cosmic body, its living self, and its indwelling controller"],["अभेदम् आरोप्य","superimposing non-difference"],["उपासनं कर्तव्यम्","worship is to be performed"],["पातालं पाद-मूलम्","Pātāla is the sole of the foot"],["पादस्याधो-भागम्","the lower part of the foot"],["पातालादीनां तद्-अवयवता","Pātāla and the rest are assigned as His limbs"],["पार्ष्णि-प्रपदे","the heel and the forepart of the foot"]],"note":""},{"canto":2,"chapter":1,"start":27,"end":27,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/01_dhyAnavidhiH.md","source_blob_sha":"14edc4de01f9e540a6c72dbdd4e4cfa009224c3c","pairs":[["ऊरु-द्वयस्याधो-भागे वितलम्","Vitala is the lower part of the two thighs"],["उत्तर-भागे अतलम्","Atala is the upper part"],["नाभिर् एव सरः","the navel itself is the lake"]],"note":""},{"canto":2,"chapter":1,"start":28,"end":28,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/01_dhyAnavidhiH.md","source_blob_sha":"14edc4de01f9e540a6c72dbdd4e4cfa009224c3c","pairs":[["ज्योतिर्-अनीकं","the host of lights"],["ज्योतिषां समूहं स्वर्गम्","the collection of luminaries, heaven"],["महर्-लोकं ग्रीवायाम्","Maharloka at the neck"],["तपो-लोकं रराटीम्","Tapoloka at the forehead"],["सत्यं सत्य-लोकम्","Satya, the world of truth"]],"note":""},{"canto":2,"chapter":1,"start":29,"end":29,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/01_dhyAnavidhiH.md","source_blob_sha":"14edc4de01f9e540a6c72dbdd4e4cfa009224c3c","pairs":[["ते बाहव इत्य् आहुः","they say these are the arms"],["दिशोऽस्मद्-आदि-श्रोत्राधिष्ठात्री देवताः","the directions are the deities presiding over hearing"],["कर्णौ श्रोत्रस्याधिष्ठानम्","the ears are the seat of hearing"],["शब्दस् तु श्रोत्र-विषयः","sound is the object of hearing"],["स तस्य श्रोत्रेन्द्रियम्","the ear is its sense organ"],["नासत्य-दस्राव् अश्विनौ","the Aśvins, Nasatya and Dasra"],["नासे नासा-पुटे","the nostrils are the openings of the nose"],["इद्धो दीप्तः","shining, brilliant"]],"note":"The pinned source begins this gloss with the damaged word “उस्रा”; that word is omitted rather than guessed. The remaining Śrīdhara gloss is retained."},{"canto":2,"chapter":1,"start":30,"end":30,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/01_dhyAnavidhiH.md","source_blob_sha":"14edc4de01f9e540a6c72dbdd4e4cfa009224c3c","pairs":[["द्यौर् अन्तरिक्षम्","heaven is midspace"],["अक्षिणी नेत्र-गोलके","the two eyes are the eyeballs"],["चक्षुर् इन्द्रियम्","sight is the sense"],["पतङ्गः सूर्यः","the moving luminary is the sun"],["अहनी रात्र्य्-अहणी","the two times are day and night"],["परमेष्ठि-धिष्ण्यं ब्रह्म-पदम्","the highest seat is Brahmā’s abode"],["तालुर् अधिष्ठानम्","the palate is the seat"],["जिह्वा इन्द्रियम्","the tongue is the sense"]],"note":""},{"canto":2,"chapter":1,"start":31,"end":31,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/01_dhyAnavidhiH.md","source_blob_sha":"14edc4de01f9e540a6c72dbdd4e4cfa009224c3c","pairs":[["छन्दांसि वेदाः","the meters are the Vedas"],["शिरो ब्रह्म-रन्ध्रम्","the head is the aperture of Brahmā"],["स्नेह-कलाः पुत्रादि-स्नेह-लेशाः","the traces of affection for sons and the like"],["द्विजानि दन्ताः","the twice-born are the teeth"],["दुरन्तोऽपारः","unfathomable, boundless"],["सर्ग इति यत्","what is called creation"]],"note":"The pinned source reads “कटाक्षह्” in this phrase, a visibly damaged ending. The phrase is omitted rather than silently normalized."},{"canto":2,"chapter":1,"start":32,"end":32,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/01_dhyAnavidhiH.md","source_blob_sha":"14edc4de01f9e540a6c72dbdd4e4cfa009224c3c","pairs":[["अधर्म-मार्गोऽस्य पृष्ठ-भागः","the path of irreligion is His back"],["कः प्रजापतिः","Ka is Prajāpati"],["मित्रौ मित्रा-वरुणौ","the two Mitras are Mitra and Varuṇa"]],"note":""},{"canto":2,"chapter":1,"start":33,"end":33,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/01_dhyAnavidhiH.md","source_blob_sha":"14edc4de01f9e540a6c72dbdd4e4cfa009224c3c","pairs":[["अनन्तं वीर्यं यस्य सः","He whose power is unlimited"],["वयः कालः","time is His movement"],["गुण-प्रवाहः","the flow of the qualities"],["प्राणिनां संसारः","the transmigration of living beings"],["कर्म तस्य क्रीडा","action is His play"]],"note":""},{"canto":2,"chapter":1,"start":34,"end":34,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/01_dhyAnavidhiH.md","source_blob_sha":"14edc4de01f9e540a6c72dbdd4e4cfa009224c3c","pairs":[["भूम्नो विभोः","of the abundant, all-pervading Lord"],["अव्यक्तं प्रधानम्","the unmanifest is primordial matter"],["चन्द्रमास् तदीयं मनः","the moon is His mind"],["सर्वेषां विकाराणां कोश इव","like the repository of all transformations"],["आश्रय-भूतम्","the underlying support"]],"note":""},{"canto":2,"chapter":1,"start":35,"end":35,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/01_dhyAnavidhiH.md","source_blob_sha":"14edc4de01f9e540a6c72dbdd4e4cfa009224c3c","pairs":[["विज्ञान-शक्तिं चित्तम्","the power of consciousness is the mind"],["महिं महत्-तत्त्वम्","the earth is the great principle"],["अन्तः-करणम् अहंकारम्","the inner instrument is ego"],["गिरित्रं श्री-रुद्रम्","Giritra is Lord Rudra"],["अश्वतरी","a female mule"]],"note":""},{"canto":2,"chapter":1,"start":36,"end":36,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/01_dhyAnavidhiH.md","source_blob_sha":"14edc4de01f9e540a6c72dbdd4e4cfa009224c3c","pairs":[["वयांसि पक्षिणः","the birds"],["व्याकरणं नाम-रूपे व्याकरवाणीति","grammar is the skill of articulating names and forms"],["शिल्प-नैपुण्यम्","skill in crafts"]],"note":""},{"canto":2,"chapter":1,"start":37,"end":37,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/01_dhyAnavidhiH.md","source_blob_sha":"14edc4de01f9e540a6c72dbdd4e4cfa009224c3c","pairs":[["ब्रह्मा विप्रः","Brahmā is the brāhmaṇa"],["तस्याननं मुखम्","His face"],["क्षत्रं क्षत्रियो भुजौ यस्य","the kṣatriya is He whose arms are the warrior class"],["विड् वैश्य ऊरू यस्य","the vaiśya is He whose thighs are the trading class"],["अङ्घ्रि-श्रितः कृष्ण-वर्णः शूद्रः","the dark-complexioned śūdra rests at His feet"],["नानाभिधा नामानि येषाम्","whose names are manifold"],["अभीज्या देवाः","the gods worthy of worship"],["वसु-रुद्रादिभिर् उपपन्नः","equipped with hosts such as the Vasus and Rudras"],["द्रव्यात्मको हविः-साध्यः","consisting of offerings and accomplished by oblations"],["वितान-योगो यज्ञ-प्रयोगः","the arrangement of the sacrifice is its ritual application"],["आवश्यकोऽभिप्रेतः","intended as necessary"]],"note":""},{"canto":2,"chapter":1,"start":38,"end":38,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/01_dhyAnavidhiH.md","source_blob_sha":"14edc4de01f9e540a6c72dbdd4e4cfa009224c3c","pairs":[["इयान् एतावान्","this much"],["सन्निवेशोऽवयव-संस्थानम्","the arrangement is the disposition of the limbs"],["अस्मिन् स्व-बुद्ध्या मनः सन्धार्यते","the mind is fixed on this by one’s own understanding"],["मुमुक्षुभिः","by those who desire liberation"],["यतो व्यतिरिक्तं किंचिन् नास्ति","because nothing exists apart from it"],["तस्मिन्","in that"]],"note":""},{"canto":2,"chapter":1,"start":39,"end":39,"source_path":"bhAgavatam/gauDIya-prastutiH/02/01_dhyAnavidhiH.md","source_blob_sha":"14edc4de01f9e540a6c72dbdd4e4cfa009224c3c","pairs":[["चित्त-स्थैर्यार्थम्","for steadiness of mind"],["विराड्-देह-जीवेश्वराणाम् अभेदेनोपासनम्","worship through non-difference of the cosmic body, living self, and Lord"],["देह-जीवाव् ईश्वरे प्रविलाप्य","having dissolved body and living self in the Lord"],["स एव ध्येयः","He alone is to be meditated upon"],["सर्वेषां धी-वृत्तिभिर् अनुभूतं सर्वम् येन","He by whom all is experienced through every movement of intelligence"],["स एक एव सर्वान्तरात्मा","He alone is the inner Self of all"],["तमेव सत्यं भजेत","one should worship Him alone as the real"],["अन्यत्र उपलक्षणे न सज्जेत्","one should not become attached to anything else"],["यतः आसङ्गाद् आत्मनः पातः संसारः भवति","for from attachment the self falls into worldly existence"],["स्वप्न-जनानाम् ईक्षिता यथा","like the observer of the people in a dream"],["ईश्वरस्य विद्या-शक्तित्वान् न बन्धः","the Lord is not bound, because He is the power of knowledge"]],"note":""}]}